1
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:33,719
We need authorization from every single investor.

2
00:00:34,039 --> 00:00:35,079
Every single one?

3
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,399
How many people is that?

4
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,439
We'd have to get everyone to sign.

5
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,560
What if even one refuses to sign?

6
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:42,159
It's all Liu Xuemei's fault.

7
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,359
The auction fell through,

8
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,359
and now she's dead.

9
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,560
We still need her authorization.

10
00:00:49,679 --> 00:00:50,439
Where on earth do we get that?

11
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,880
Hire a shaman to summon her spirit?

12
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:54,600
Why'd you kick me?

13
00:00:54,799 --> 00:00:55,439
Cut the crap, both of you.

14
00:00:55,439 --> 00:00:56,119
Am I wrong?

15
00:00:56,119 --> 00:00:57,280
You're talking complete nonsense.

16
00:00:57,679 --> 00:00:58,520
If you ask me,

17
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,679
why don't we forge her signature?

18
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:01,840
We sign it for her.

19
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,920
Make it look messy on purpose.

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,760
If anyone asks,

21
00:01:04,879 --> 00:01:05,840
we just say the ink smudged.

22
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:06,680
Right!

23
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,519
Are you an idiot?

24
00:01:07,519 --> 00:01:08,879
Give it a rest, will you?

25
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,560
You think the auction folks are stupid?

26
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:11,439
Then what do we do?

27
00:01:12,079 --> 00:01:13,319
What about my money?

28
00:01:13,959 --> 00:01:14,359
Move, get back!

29
00:01:14,359 --> 00:01:14,879
Don't start that here.

30
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,200
Worst comes to worst, I'll sue them in court!

31
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:18,239
Right?

32
00:01:18,239 --> 00:01:19,079
Sue who?

33
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,319
Go to court?

34
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:21,640
Aren't you afraid of getting exposed now?

35
00:01:21,799 --> 00:01:23,480
Are you completely out of your mind?

36
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,200
Do you have any idea?

37
00:01:24,239 --> 00:01:26,319
Lawsuits drag on forever!

38
00:01:26,599 --> 00:01:27,799
Before the case even ends,

39
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:28,640
you'll be laid off!

40
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,799
You get it, dummy?

41
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,159
The factory will be gone,

42
00:01:31,159 --> 00:01:32,159
the money will be gone,

43
00:01:32,159 --> 00:01:34,480
and we'll have lost everything!

44
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:36,480
No matter what,

45
00:01:37,319 --> 00:01:38,200
the list cannot be leaked.

46
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:41,200
Our coworkers trusted us

47
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:42,079
and loved the factory,

48
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:44,040
that's why they put in their life savings.

49
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:44,760
That's right.

50
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,239
And if this list gets out,

51
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:46,959
let me tell you,

52
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:48,519
it'll turn straight into a layoff list!

53
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,519
You believe that?

54
00:01:49,519 --> 00:01:51,680
What if the auction company sold us out?

55
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,480
They're bound by strict confidentiality.

56
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,959
Breaching that means paying damages!

57
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:55,760
I don't care about any list!

58
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,719
I just want my money!

59
00:01:56,799 --> 00:01:57,159
Money!

60
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,159
Money, money, money!

61
00:01:58,159 --> 00:01:59,280
Money is all you ever think about!

62
00:01:59,879 --> 00:02:00,599
If we get laid off,

63
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,840
someone like you won't starve!

64
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,920
Neither of you will starve!

65
00:02:03,239 --> 00:02:04,319
What about my coworkers?

66
00:02:04,599 --> 00:02:05,200
What will they eat?

67
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:06,439
What will their wives eat?

68
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:07,079
What will their kids eat?

69
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:08,120
What will their families eat?

70
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:08,879
Chunyan!

71
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,159
What are you eating?

72
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,080
The fundraising list!

73
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:16,680
The list!

74
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:17,960
Chunyan!

75
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,360
Spit it out, quick!

76
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:19,879
You can't eat that!

77
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:20,719
Chunyan, spit it out!

78
00:02:20,759 --> 00:02:21,520
Water, water, water!

79
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,599
Don't give her water! No water!

80
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,199
Chunyan! Chunyan! Chunyan!

81
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:26,599
Spit it out!

82
00:02:26,599 --> 00:02:27,240
Enough!

83
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,560
Quit panicking!

84
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,479
Take her to the clinic right away!

85
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:32,240
Wait! Hold on!

86
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,240
Pumping her stomach will expose the list!

87
00:02:34,599 --> 00:02:35,360
Well... then...

88
00:02:37,479 --> 00:02:38,560
I swallowed it.

89
00:04:21,439 --> 00:04:22,319
Xiao Tu,

90
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:24,240
you're still too impulsive.

91
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:26,839
What's the point of eating just the list?

92
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:28,279
Isn't there still a ledger?

93
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,519
Can't you just shut up?

94
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:33,959
Chunyan did it for all of us!

95
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:35,920
If you get her all worked up

96
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,079
and she eats the ledger, it's on you!

97
00:04:44,279 --> 00:04:45,720
I've got a win-win solution.

98
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,959
We still take the money.

99
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,680
Take the cash and wait at home.

100
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,600
A strike?

101
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:55,600
Exactly.

102
00:04:56,759 --> 00:04:57,480
With nobody working,

103
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,360
the plant will shut down.

104
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,399
Then he'll definitely have to

105
00:05:00,399 --> 00:05:01,399
beg everyone back one by one.

106
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,319
Don't you want the money?

107
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:04,480
Let's go.

108
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,439
Well... but...

109
00:05:07,439 --> 00:05:08,439
Shun'er and I will go get—

110
00:05:08,439 --> 00:05:09,160
Where are you two going?

111
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:11,000
To sort out the authorization.

112
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:11,920
Sit down first.

113
00:05:13,319 --> 00:05:14,399
He's a college grad.

114
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,920
He can find a job anywhere.

115
00:05:16,199 --> 00:05:17,240
Where will you two go if you're laid off?

116
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:19,920
Besides,

117
00:05:21,319 --> 00:05:23,639
how long can you hold onto this iron rice bowl?

118
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,800
How long will this little bit of cash last?

119
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,079
Don't you two have any clue?

120
00:05:27,879 --> 00:05:28,600
Wait, but...

121
00:05:28,959 --> 00:05:29,879
what about the money?

122
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,839
What about it?

123
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,000
Let me make my stance clear.

124
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,240
I don't want the money anymore.

125
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,480
Wait, but you just—

126
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,120
Fine if you don't want it!

127
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:36,600
What about my money?

128
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,120
That's my entire life savings!

129
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,639
You can't just be so shortsighted.

130
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:40,439
All my money's gone right now! Alright, alright.

131
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:41,199
Both of you, cut it out.

132
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:41,800
Enough.

133
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,160
Just keep it down.

134
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,720
What's the point

135
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,279
of us bickering like this?

136
00:05:48,399 --> 00:05:50,360
So many people pooled their money with us.

137
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,040
Shouldn't we see what everyone wants?

138
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:54,800
Right.

139
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:57,000
We have to find a way

140
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,959
to get everyone's money

141
00:06:00,639 --> 00:06:01,279
all back first.

142
00:06:01,639 --> 00:06:02,800
Then we can talk about

143
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,959
whether the list gets exposed.

144
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,040
Old Chen is right.

145
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:08,639
Right?

146
00:06:08,639 --> 00:06:10,560
I—I say let's take a show of hands.

147
00:06:10,759 --> 00:06:11,199
Well...

148
00:06:11,199 --> 00:06:12,079
for the forklift crew...

149
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:12,800
We... we want the money.

150
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,759
Workshop Two wants the money, too!

151
00:06:28,399 --> 00:06:29,000
Tieping.

152
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,639
Stop playing dumb.

153
00:06:33,519 --> 00:06:34,720
What's your side thinking?

154
00:06:36,959 --> 00:06:37,639
Don't ask me.

155
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,959
I just do what my mentor says.

156
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,199
Look,

157
00:06:52,319 --> 00:06:53,519
to put it bluntly,

158
00:06:54,879 --> 00:06:55,839
that money

159
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:58,079
is everything Tieping and I

160
00:06:58,879 --> 00:06:59,879
have in the world.

161
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:02,519
Forget about me.

162
00:07:03,439 --> 00:07:05,439
Just take the five thousand Tieping scraped together.

163
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:10,240
Think of how many crates of beer

164
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,319
he had to haul to make that!

165
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:14,199
Right?

166
00:07:17,199 --> 00:07:18,319
You want your money back,

167
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,279
and so do I.

168
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:23,680
But today,

169
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,680
if this list is handed over,

170
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,199
what will happen to Tieping?

171
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,240
Besides,

172
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,720
on that list,

173
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,120
folks from the bottling workshop,

174
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:36,560
there are plenty of them, right?

175
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:39,920
Among them,

176
00:07:40,519 --> 00:07:41,639
some I watched join the plant,

177
00:07:44,639 --> 00:07:45,959
and some watched me join.

178
00:07:47,879 --> 00:07:49,199
Now you're telling me

179
00:07:49,319 --> 00:07:51,040
they can't stay at the plant anymore?

180
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,360
They have no other skills.

181
00:07:56,079 --> 00:07:57,040
What will they live on?

182
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:01,480
Sure,

183
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,360
three or five thousand

184
00:08:06,199 --> 00:08:07,000
is a lot of money.

185
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,519
Tell me,

186
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,720
with just a few thousand,

187
00:08:13,519 --> 00:08:14,560
can they really

188
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,439
make it last until they die?

189
00:08:18,079 --> 00:08:18,680
Can they?

190
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,160
Sit down.

191
00:08:22,839 --> 00:08:23,439
Qian Yichuan,

192
00:08:24,839 --> 00:08:26,120
you started this, didn't you?

193
00:08:27,279 --> 00:08:27,879
I did.

194
00:08:30,839 --> 00:08:31,920
You went to college.

195
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:33,519
You're educated.

196
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,799
You conned us onto your rocket ship.

197
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,240
You have a parachute,

198
00:08:39,279 --> 00:08:40,919
while the rest of us fall to our deaths!

199
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,879
What are you really planning?

200
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,320
Now you're duping everyone

201
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,799
into going on strike!

202
00:08:47,559 --> 00:08:48,320
What's your angle?

203
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,559
If everyone gets laid off,

204
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,200
what do you get out of it?

205
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,200
You want to be the plant director?

206
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:56,559
Qian Yichuan,

207
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,080
you don't deserve to work at Lapi Brewery!

208
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,720
Lao Cheng, Lao Cheng!

209
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,080
Calm down, take it easy!

210
00:09:04,639 --> 00:09:05,159
Sit, sit, sit.

211
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:05,759
Sit down.

212
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,440
Sit down.

213
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:13,759
Bottling workshop!

214
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,279
Back to work!

215
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:28,519
Hey,

216
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:29,799
forklift crew, let's get back to work too.

217
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:30,720
You want to get laid off?

218
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:31,080
Get moving!

219
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:34,759
Liuzi!

220
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,320
Your place got broken into?

221
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:13,879
I need to head out for a while.

222
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,480
These things...

223
00:10:16,559 --> 00:10:17,600
...still mean something to me.

224
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,960
I'll leave them with you for now.

225
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,720
When did it happen?

226
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,120
The night before last.

227
00:10:22,279 --> 00:10:23,120
The night before last?

228
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,279
Weren't you at my place?

229
00:10:24,679 --> 00:10:25,639
What did they steal?

230
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:28,039
Discarded footage from Lapi Brewery.

231
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:31,919
You still kept that?

232
00:10:33,919 --> 00:10:35,600
Why would anyone steal that?

233
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,600
Who did it?

234
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,240
Who else could it be?

235
00:10:39,759 --> 00:10:40,360
Who?

236
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:44,519
Leshui is here.

237
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,039
I came to see Xiaoqin and Xiaohu.

238
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,440
Have you eaten yet?

239
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:49,480
Stay for dinner before you go.

240
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,919
Why are you home so early today?

241
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,799
Exams are over,

242
00:10:54,919 --> 00:10:56,320
so school let out early.

243
00:10:58,639 --> 00:10:59,480
What's there to eat?

244
00:10:59,919 --> 00:11:00,440
I'm starving.

245
00:11:01,399 --> 00:11:01,919
Let me take that.

246
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:03,639
I'll leave you to it, then.

247
00:11:03,799 --> 00:11:04,360
I'm heading back.

248
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:05,240
Leaving already?

249
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:05,639
Chen Yuan.

250
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,120
Help Leshui take the box...

251
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,120
...down to the storage room.

252
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:08,840
Sure.

253
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,639
You called the other day saying your camera broke.

254
00:11:11,639 --> 00:11:12,120
Here.

255
00:11:12,679 --> 00:11:14,279
I was going to have Chen Yuan fix it for you.

256
00:11:14,279 --> 00:11:15,000
No need to fix it.

257
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:15,919
I'll just buy a new one.

258
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:17,240
Leshui.

259
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,720
It'll be safe here, don't worry.

260
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,720
Thanks.

261
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:20,480
I'm off.

262
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,240
Miss,

263
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:34,919
what can I get you?

264
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,360
Do you have a machine here

265
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,200
that can play this kind of tape?

266
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:42,320
Yeah.

267
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:53,120
For an old tape like this,

268
00:11:53,159 --> 00:11:54,639
only this kind of player will work.

269
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:56,960
Over the past couple of days,

270
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,679
has anyone bought one of these?

271
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:01,080
I think one person did.

272
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,360
What did he look like?

273
00:12:03,039 --> 00:12:04,759
About thirty or so.

274
00:12:04,879 --> 00:12:05,759
Average build.

275
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:06,639
A bit taller than me.

276
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,159
Did he look like a cop?

277
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,360
A cop?

278
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,519
Why are you asking?

279
00:12:12,679 --> 00:12:14,679
Just worried I'd buy the same thing as my brother.

280
00:12:17,759 --> 00:12:18,480
Sorry about that.

281
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,240
Thank you.

282
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,399
Hey, were you looking for me?

283
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:29,960
Hey,

284
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:30,919
today I ran into

285
00:12:30,919 --> 00:12:32,159
Miao from the station back then.

286
00:12:32,799 --> 00:12:33,519
Miao Yuzhu.

287
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:34,120
Remember her?

288
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:35,360
She said back then,

289
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,840
she worked with you on Malt Kingdom,

290
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,159
helping sort through footage.

291
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:38,679
Director Zheng...

292
00:12:38,679 --> 00:12:39,559
She slipped you three extra tapes. You called me?

293
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:40,399
Xiao Miao...

294
00:12:40,399 --> 00:12:41,240
She did it behind the boss's back.

295
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,080
You took her to fetch the tapes,

296
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,200
so she's really fond of you.

297
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,080
Miao runs a self-media account now.

298
00:12:45,159 --> 00:12:47,320
Almost every article gets over 100k views.

299
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:47,960
She said

300
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:50,080
if you have any explosive scoops,

301
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,440
she'd love to publish them for us.

302
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:55,559
I never even considered that.

303
00:12:56,679 --> 00:12:58,320
Lives are on the line here.

304
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,279
Investigating is fine,

305
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,200
but we can't interfere with police work.

306
00:13:03,039 --> 00:13:04,759
As journalists, we must be responsible.

307
00:13:06,679 --> 00:13:07,480
Got it.

308
00:13:07,879 --> 00:13:08,679
That you're willing to mentor me...

309
00:13:08,679 --> 00:13:09,679
I'm truly touched.

310
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,919
Don't worry about it.

311
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,320
From now on, I'll do whatever you say.

312
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,159
Wherever you point, that's where I'll go.

313
00:13:14,519 --> 00:13:15,440
I'm heading to Qingzhou now.

314
00:13:15,559 --> 00:13:16,360
Then I'll come with you.

315
00:13:16,799 --> 00:13:17,279
No need.

316
00:13:18,039 --> 00:13:18,519
Alright.

317
00:13:18,879 --> 00:13:19,919
Just stay safe.

318
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,159
If I can't reach you for two hours,

319
00:13:21,159 --> 00:13:21,840
I'm calling the cops.

320
00:13:21,919 --> 00:13:22,639
Dramatic.

321
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,039
We'll talk when I'm back.

322
00:13:47,519 --> 00:13:48,320
Anyone home?

323
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,480
Who are you looking for?

324
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,679
I was just about to head out,

325
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,799
and here you are.

326
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:58,720
Come on in.

327
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,960
My grandson Xuelin,

328
00:14:01,519 --> 00:14:03,279
is really something, you know?

329
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:06,879
Even got a reporter here to interview him.

330
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,080
Come on, sit right here.

331
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:09,639
Have a seat.

332
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:11,279
Make yourself at home.

333
00:14:11,879 --> 00:14:13,440
Let me get you some water.

334
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:14,879
On such a freezing day,

335
00:14:14,879 --> 00:14:16,080
coming all this way.

336
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,200
Thank you.

337
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:17,879
Sit here.

338
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,159
Go ahead, sit, sit.

339
00:14:19,159 --> 00:14:19,720
All right, take a seat.

340
00:14:29,879 --> 00:14:30,759
Here, have some water.

341
00:14:31,519 --> 00:14:31,840
Here you go.

342
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:33,919
Thank you.

343
00:14:34,799 --> 00:14:35,720
Looking at photos?

344
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,399
There are more here.

345
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,759
Lots of them.

346
00:14:40,759 --> 00:14:42,120
They're all family photos of his.

347
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,200
They turned out great.

348
00:14:43,879 --> 00:14:44,399
Take a look.

349
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,279
Look how cute he was as a kid.

350
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:56,000
The boy's had a rough life, really.

351
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:57,639
You know...

352
00:14:58,039 --> 00:14:59,679
His dad was busy all day,

353
00:14:59,759 --> 00:15:00,879
rushing off his feet.

354
00:15:00,879 --> 00:15:02,120
Nobody looked after the boy.

355
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,039
So just like that,

356
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,159
he was sent over to stay with me.

357
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,519
I didn't have fancy food either.

358
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,519
I just made corn grits porridge.

359
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:12,600
Eating that corn grits porridge, he said,

360
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,000
"This stuff of yours,

361
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,200
it scratches my throat.

362
00:15:15,679 --> 00:15:17,279
I can't swallow it," you know?

363
00:15:20,919 --> 00:15:23,440
It really cracked me up!

364
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:25,679
He ate so slowly.

365
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:27,200
When I nagged him a bit,

366
00:15:27,759 --> 00:15:28,519
oh boy,

367
00:15:28,879 --> 00:15:29,720
he started crying.

368
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:32,360
He was very proud.

369
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,720
Couldn't take any criticism.

370
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:38,039
Grandma, here.

371
00:15:38,279 --> 00:15:38,919
Sit here.

372
00:15:38,919 --> 00:15:39,240
Please, have a seat.

373
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,159
I'm interviewing you, look at me...

374
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:40,720
Please sit down.

375
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,600
You're interviewing me?

376
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:41,960
Yes.

377
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:42,600
Alright.

378
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:43,120
Please sit, take a seat.

379
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,200
Let's have a nice chat.

380
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:44,919
Come on.

381
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:47,840
Mrs. Gao, I'll take some notes, okay?

382
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:48,360
Sure.

383
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,759
What was Gao Xuelin's personality like?

384
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,279
He didn't talk much.

385
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,799
Even though he stayed quiet

386
00:15:56,799 --> 00:15:57,840
and kept to himself,

387
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:59,320
he had quite a mind of his own.

388
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:02,080
Did he go to school locally?

389
00:16:02,559 --> 00:16:04,320
He went to college right here.

390
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:05,720
Didn't go elsewhere.

391
00:16:06,159 --> 00:16:08,399
Has he been to Lacheng, then?

392
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,480
Him?

393
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,480
He went to Lacheng all the time!

394
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,480
Good grief,

395
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,600
non-stop!

396
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:14,600
You wouldn't believe it.

397
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,679
What did he go there for?

398
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:16,679
For what?

399
00:16:16,679 --> 00:16:17,679
He wouldn't let anyone ask!

400
00:16:18,559 --> 00:16:19,399
If you asked,

401
00:16:19,399 --> 00:16:20,559
he'd get upset.

402
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,840
He always told me,

403
00:16:22,559 --> 00:16:24,360
"Don't bother worrying about it."

404
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:26,960
That's what he'd say.

405
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,480
It's only because you're here...

406
00:16:31,879 --> 00:16:32,399
Mrs. Gao,

407
00:16:33,639 --> 00:16:35,080
I was looking at the photos earlier.

408
00:16:36,159 --> 00:16:36,799
Um...

409
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,639
Gao Xuelin's mother,

410
00:16:38,679 --> 00:16:39,480
which

411
00:16:39,639 --> 00:16:40,399
one was she?

412
00:16:40,759 --> 00:16:41,399
I'll find it for you.

413
00:16:41,639 --> 00:16:42,200
Here it is.

414
00:16:44,519 --> 00:16:45,000
This one.

415
00:16:45,799 --> 00:16:46,360
Take a look.

416
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,360
She was such a gorgeous woman.

417
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:52,120
And such a good person too.

418
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,000
Giving birth to him, though,

419
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,279
she suffered massive bleeding.

420
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,159
Just like that, she was gone.

421
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,480
It broke my heart so much.

422
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,720
And...

423
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,839
what about Gao Xuelin's father?

424
00:17:13,759 --> 00:17:17,119
His father was a taxi driver.

425
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,279
Got into a car crash that year,

426
00:17:19,519 --> 00:17:20,400
and passed away too.

427
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,319
Child,

428
00:17:29,559 --> 00:17:30,720
remember this:

429
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:33,519
never drink and drive.

430
00:17:33,519 --> 00:17:34,920
It's devastating!

431
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:37,640
Right.

432
00:17:47,759 --> 00:17:49,359
Since you're here today,

433
00:17:49,599 --> 00:17:50,720
I won't stand on ceremony.

434
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,720
I'd like to ask you a favor.

435
00:17:54,319 --> 00:17:55,000
Go ahead.

436
00:17:55,319 --> 00:17:57,920
You see that big smokestack on the east end?

437
00:17:58,519 --> 00:17:59,880
The factory's gone,

438
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,640
all shut down,

439
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,680
yet that smokestack is still standing.

440
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:03,519
You...

441
00:18:03,839 --> 00:18:07,079
You meet a lot of big shots,

442
00:18:07,319 --> 00:18:09,039
and you can talk to them.

443
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:11,079
Tell those officials

444
00:18:11,519 --> 00:18:12,880
to tear down that smokestack.

445
00:18:13,599 --> 00:18:14,200
Could you?

446
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:15,119
Grandma...

447
00:18:15,119 --> 00:18:15,440
Can you?

448
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:18,480
You want me to report on that smokestack?

449
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:19,279
No.

450
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:23,920
Don't you deal with big shots all the time?

451
00:18:24,599 --> 00:18:26,400
Where else am I supposed to find them?

452
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,359
Tearing down a smokestack,

453
00:18:29,359 --> 00:18:31,240
how hard could that be for them?

454
00:18:31,559 --> 00:18:35,440
You... you even wrote an article on Xuelin.

455
00:18:39,839 --> 00:18:40,400
Mrs. Gao,

456
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,400
where does Xuelin stay?

457
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,079
Can I take a look inside his room?

458
00:18:45,519 --> 00:18:46,480
It's right in that room.

459
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:47,839
Come on, I'll show you.

460
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:55,880
Take a look.

461
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,039
This is his room.

462
00:19:02,319 --> 00:19:03,720
You rest here, okay?

463
00:19:03,759 --> 00:19:05,519
I'll make you pickled cabbage dumplings,

464
00:19:05,559 --> 00:19:06,079
how about that?

465
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:07,440
Don't trouble yourself.

466
00:19:08,039 --> 00:19:08,440
Don't worry about it.

467
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,559
Come on, have a seat.

468
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:31,720
Dad, I got you!

469
00:21:36,519 --> 00:21:37,759
Dad, I won!

470
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:46,720
Good job.

471
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:51,279
Dad, aren't you eating?

472
00:21:51,359 --> 00:21:53,519
Daddy's got a big job to run today.

473
00:21:53,559 --> 00:21:54,480
To make some good money.

474
00:21:54,759 --> 00:21:56,880
I'll buy you a big toy gun when I'm back.

475
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:58,480
Yay!

476
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,480
Will you be back tonight?

477
00:22:00,759 --> 00:22:01,519
You bet.

478
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,200
We've gotta spend New Year's together.

479
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,279
Okay!

480
00:22:04,279 --> 00:22:04,799
Go on inside.

481
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:05,920
Eat with Grandma, okay?

482
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,880
Come back soon!

483
00:22:08,079 --> 00:22:08,599
Will do.

484
00:22:15,359 --> 00:22:16,200
Dad!

485
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,759
Grandma told me to give you a meat bun.

486
00:22:35,559 --> 00:22:36,480
Did you find his place?

487
00:22:38,799 --> 00:22:40,279
Was the tip I gave you useful?

488
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:41,599
Find anything new?

489
00:22:48,079 --> 00:22:50,839
December 31, 1999.

490
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:54,559
Beer taster Liu Xuemei froze to death after drinking.

491
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:58,200
December 31, 1999.

492
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,799
Taxi driver Gao so-and-so

493
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,279
died in a drunk driving crash. Hello?

494
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:03,200
Hello?

495
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,200
Are you listening?

496
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:08,200
They actually died on the very same day.

497
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:10,440
Hello?

498
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:16,160
Could that really be a coincidence?

499
00:23:16,799 --> 00:23:17,839
What did you find?

500
00:23:17,839 --> 00:23:18,640
I'll tell you when I get back.

501
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:21,559
Liu Xuemei...

502
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,440
What really happened that day?

503
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,839
Xuemei! Xuemei!

504
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:36,599
Leshui.

505
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:37,519
Xuemei!

506
00:23:37,759 --> 00:23:38,640
You made it.

507
00:23:40,319 --> 00:23:41,720
I took a cab from Qingzhou.

508
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:42,839
That's great.

509
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:44,480
Hurry and go inside, Xuemei.

510
00:23:44,559 --> 00:23:45,480
I'll wait for your good news.

511
00:23:49,079 --> 00:23:50,039
Good luck, Xuemei!

512
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:07,319
Shen!

513
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:10,119
Let me take that.

514
00:24:10,119 --> 00:24:10,559
I've got it.

515
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:12,319
Why take a train at this hour?

516
00:24:12,319 --> 00:24:12,799
I was in a rush.

517
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:13,880
Caught the earliest one.

518
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:14,799
What's the big rush?

519
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,480
Let's talk in the car.

520
00:24:16,119 --> 00:24:16,599
Right here.

521
00:24:17,039 --> 00:24:17,640
Get in.

522
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:24,799
I was wrong before.

523
00:24:25,559 --> 00:24:26,559
He's investigating this

524
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:29,119
because he suspects Gao Wusong's death

525
00:24:29,279 --> 00:24:30,519
was tied to Liu Xuemei.

526
00:24:31,079 --> 00:24:32,000
His real target

527
00:24:32,279 --> 00:24:33,759
were the tapes I shot back then.

528
00:24:34,079 --> 00:24:35,400
He definitely stole those videotapes.

529
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,160
Now I know why he stole them too.

530
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:39,440
He suspects Liu Xuemei

531
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,519
was riding in his dad's car.

532
00:24:45,039 --> 00:24:46,400
I found this at his place.

533
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:48,200
I checked with the auction house.

534
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:50,680
They said in '99, to mark the millennium,

535
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,119
they made custom bidding paddles.

536
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,880
On December 31st,

537
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,119
Gao Wusong went to Lacheng.

538
00:24:55,519 --> 00:24:57,680
Lacheng only had one auction that day.

539
00:24:59,359 --> 00:25:00,200
So he suspects

540
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:02,160
his dad drove Liu Xuemei that day.

541
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:02,640
Right.

542
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:04,440
At least,

543
00:25:04,599 --> 00:25:05,920
that's what Gao Xuelin thinks.

544
00:25:06,039 --> 00:25:06,839
He even tracked down

545
00:25:06,839 --> 00:25:08,599
a matching paddle from that auction.

546
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:10,839
It's probably not Liu Xuemei's paddle,

547
00:25:11,079 --> 00:25:12,160
but it clearly shows

548
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,480
Gao Xuelin's line of investigation.

549
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,119
Is Liu Xuemei's death

550
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:19,000
tied to Gao Wusong?

551
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:20,720
Or

552
00:25:21,599 --> 00:25:23,400
were they murdered together?

553
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,839
Liu Xuemei's death is tied to a cop's dad.

554
00:25:28,319 --> 00:25:28,920
Shen,

555
00:25:29,279 --> 00:25:30,720
this is huge news.

556
00:25:31,119 --> 00:25:32,119
It could easily make front page.

557
00:25:35,039 --> 00:25:35,480
Let's go.

558
00:25:38,079 --> 00:25:39,319
A serial murder case...

559
00:25:40,599 --> 00:25:42,319
Could it be linked to the past?

560
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,240
How did they die?

561
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,480
They're all the old-timers from back then.

562
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,599
They moved out later on.

563
00:25:50,599 --> 00:25:51,200
Officer Gao.

564
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,440
Got a minute to talk?

565
00:25:53,359 --> 00:25:55,759
Anything else you saw or noticed,

566
00:25:55,759 --> 00:25:56,440
feel free to tell us.

567
00:25:58,319 --> 00:25:59,160
Think carefully about it.

568
00:25:59,160 --> 00:25:59,960
I thought about it, but didn't notice anything.

569
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:00,559
Right?

570
00:26:01,559 --> 00:26:02,240
Well,

571
00:26:02,759 --> 00:26:03,519
if you happen to recall

572
00:26:03,519 --> 00:26:05,759
any details later on,

573
00:26:05,759 --> 00:26:06,240
or anything at all,

574
00:26:06,519 --> 00:26:07,720
just get in touch with us.

575
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,799
Did you spot any suspicious people?

576
00:26:09,799 --> 00:26:10,759
No, not at all.

577
00:26:11,519 --> 00:26:12,240
I moved out long ago.

578
00:26:12,559 --> 00:26:13,559
Haven't lived here in ages.

579
00:26:16,079 --> 00:26:16,920
I don't know the details.

580
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,279
Please give it some more thought.

581
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,240
Reporter Shen.

582
00:26:56,519 --> 00:26:57,880
Qingzhou is colder than Lacheng, right?

583
00:26:59,559 --> 00:27:00,079
It's all right.

584
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:01,720
Your grandma was very welcoming.

585
00:27:04,559 --> 00:27:05,759
Investigating at my place,

586
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:07,200
did you find anything new?

587
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,000
Any progress on the break-in at my place?

588
00:27:11,359 --> 00:27:11,920
We're still looking into it.

589
00:27:13,519 --> 00:27:14,079
Real efficient.

590
00:27:15,519 --> 00:27:16,039
Tell you what.

591
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,640
Let me first share some of

592
00:27:19,319 --> 00:27:20,519
the things I uncovered.

593
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:26,279
Your father was Gao Wusong.

594
00:27:26,839 --> 00:27:27,920
A taxi driver.

595
00:27:28,359 --> 00:27:29,799
Born in 1964.

596
00:27:30,359 --> 00:27:32,400
On December 31, 1999,

597
00:27:32,599 --> 00:27:34,119
he died in a traffic accident.

598
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,119
He was only 36.

599
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:38,920
The crash happened on Ring Road in Lacheng.

600
00:27:39,799 --> 00:27:41,960
That day, he took a long-distance fare.

601
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:45,079
A woman rushed from Qingzhou to Lacheng

602
00:27:45,079 --> 00:27:46,519
to attend an auction.

603
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:49,720
The passenger's name was Liu Xuemei.

604
00:27:51,319 --> 00:27:52,279
I checked the gas stations

605
00:27:52,279 --> 00:27:53,880
along the route from Qingzhou to Lacheng.

606
00:27:54,519 --> 00:27:57,079
An old employee recognized your father.

607
00:27:58,039 --> 00:27:59,079
That day, he saw

608
00:27:59,079 --> 00:28:01,119
a pretty female passenger sitting in the car.

609
00:28:02,599 --> 00:28:03,599
Have something hot to eat.

610
00:28:04,799 --> 00:28:05,440
Thank you.

611
00:28:06,119 --> 00:28:07,400
We've still got a long way to go.

612
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,519
That night, Liu Xuemei

613
00:28:23,519 --> 00:28:25,400
was at a phone booth on Xingfu Road

614
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:27,720
and died of hypothermia after drinking.

615
00:28:28,559 --> 00:28:30,079
Your father, on Huandao Road,

616
00:28:30,079 --> 00:28:31,920
died from drunk driving.

617
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:34,079
They died on the very same day,

618
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,519
both drunk.

619
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:40,640
What else?

620
00:28:44,359 --> 00:28:46,599
There are two reasons you care about Liu Xuemei's death.

621
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:47,839
First,

622
00:28:48,279 --> 00:28:50,759
your dad and Liu Xuemei argued in the car,

623
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,599
which ended up causing her death,

624
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,799
and then your father got into a car crash.

625
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:57,920
Maybe someone at the brewery

626
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:59,319
found out about what happened,

627
00:29:00,079 --> 00:29:00,799
so

628
00:29:01,319 --> 00:29:03,799
you're covering up the truth for your father.

629
00:29:05,039 --> 00:29:05,720
Second,

630
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:07,759
Liu Xuemei did something

631
00:29:08,319 --> 00:29:10,000
that caused your father's car crash,

632
00:29:10,079 --> 00:29:11,119
and this whole thing

633
00:29:11,319 --> 00:29:12,799
was tied to the brewery buyout.

634
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:15,279
So you're tracking down everyone involved.

635
00:29:15,519 --> 00:29:17,559
Then I suddenly dug into this case,

636
00:29:17,799 --> 00:29:19,559
and you thought my discarded footage

637
00:29:19,559 --> 00:29:21,039
held secrets from back then.

638
00:29:21,559 --> 00:29:22,279
That's why

639
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:25,039
you stole my tapes.

640
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,680
Spoken like a true award-winning reporter.

641
00:29:40,839 --> 00:29:41,680
Nice story you spun.

642
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,119
Trying to bait me, huh?

643
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:45,039
You

644
00:29:45,039 --> 00:29:46,480
didn't even give me a heads-up

645
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:48,039
before showing up at my place

646
00:29:48,519 --> 00:29:49,519
and bothering my grandma.

647
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:50,799
A bit out of line, isn't it?

648
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,200
In here,

649
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,400
there might be leads on the burglary at your place.

650
00:29:56,319 --> 00:29:57,240
I'll take it back to look into it.

651
00:29:57,359 --> 00:29:58,000
I'll return it when I'm done.

652
00:29:59,079 --> 00:30:00,480
Didn't you see it last time?

653
00:30:01,079 --> 00:30:02,480
Why didn't you report it to your bosses?

654
00:30:03,359 --> 00:30:04,319
Got a guilty conscience?

655
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:06,160
I have no idea what you're talking about.

656
00:30:08,519 --> 00:30:09,480
Give me back the tape.

657
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:12,039
Just because I wanted to see your tape,

658
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:13,279
you can't say I stole it.

659
00:30:13,799 --> 00:30:14,880
Isn't that just framing me?

660
00:30:23,799 --> 00:30:24,799
Here's my phone number.

661
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:26,920
It's on 24/7.

662
00:30:27,279 --> 00:30:29,039
So if you have questions, just ask me directly.

663
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,759
They're almost done questioning downstairs.

664
00:31:03,359 --> 00:31:04,160
Eat, eat, eat.

665
00:31:05,640 --> 00:31:06,440
You're back?

666
00:31:07,599 --> 00:31:09,119
Isn't she the one who filmed us?

667
00:31:09,119 --> 00:31:09,960
Reporter Shen?

668
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:10,880
It really is her.

669
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:12,400
Mr. Sun.

670
00:31:13,039 --> 00:31:13,680
Mr. Li.

671
00:31:14,759 --> 00:31:15,359
Mr. Ge.

672
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:17,640
Reporter Shen!

673
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:18,359
After all these years,

674
00:31:18,359 --> 00:31:20,000
you still remember us old guys?

675
00:31:20,079 --> 00:31:20,960
How could I forget?

676
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:21,839
Of course I remember you.

677
00:31:21,839 --> 00:31:22,920
Look, you've lost your teeth.

678
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:23,759
What's become of you?

679
00:31:23,759 --> 00:31:24,480
I remember you, too.

680
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:25,200
Stop ragging on me.

681
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:25,920
Look at you.

682
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:26,839
What happened to you?

683
00:31:27,079 --> 00:31:27,759
You're totally bald!

684
00:31:28,039 --> 00:31:29,000
Bald as can be.

685
00:31:30,119 --> 00:31:31,200
Don't pick on Old Ge.

686
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:31,759
Look at you,

687
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:34,200
your hair's too thin to even mention.

688
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:35,559
What are you doing?

689
00:31:35,599 --> 00:31:37,000
A pretty reporter is right here.

690
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:37,839
Mind your manners!

691
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:39,119
I forgot for a second.

692
00:31:39,119 --> 00:31:39,759
Let me fix it.

693
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:43,279
Reporter Shen.

694
00:31:44,359 --> 00:31:45,200
Director Cheng.

695
00:31:45,599 --> 00:31:46,480
Long time no see.

696
00:31:47,279 --> 00:31:48,480
I haven't been director for years.

697
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:49,759
How's your health?

698
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,079
Good, very good.

699
00:31:52,119 --> 00:31:53,079
When did you get back?

700
00:31:53,359 --> 00:31:54,200
Just a couple of days ago.

701
00:31:57,920 --> 00:31:59,279
You say the days are long,

702
00:31:59,279 --> 00:32:00,480
so I pass the liquor along.

703
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:01,640
How's that?

704
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:04,000
Great, damn great!

705
00:32:04,319 --> 00:32:05,200
I made that up myself.

706
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:07,880
Well, you see,

707
00:32:08,039 --> 00:32:08,920
after we got laid off,

708
00:32:09,279 --> 00:32:10,359
us old guys

709
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:12,039
had nowhere to drink and chat.

710
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:13,799
So we

711
00:32:13,799 --> 00:32:14,920
took this rundown place,

712
00:32:14,920 --> 00:32:15,920
cleaned it all up,

713
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:18,039
and gave these drunks a place to hang out.

714
00:32:19,079 --> 00:32:21,880
Outsiders call it Old Drunkards' Paradise,

715
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:24,920
but we call it Old Workmates' Paradise.

716
00:32:26,640 --> 00:32:26,920
Come on.

717
00:32:27,119 --> 00:32:28,039
Come on inside, please.

718
00:32:28,119 --> 00:32:28,839
Right this way.

719
00:32:29,079 --> 00:32:29,759
There's a seat here!

720
00:32:29,759 --> 00:32:30,559
Sit here and drink with us!

721
00:32:30,759 --> 00:32:31,240
Reporter Shen,

722
00:32:32,359 --> 00:32:32,960
have a drink, have some!

723
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:33,960
Can't you shut your trap?

724
00:32:34,119 --> 00:32:34,759
Go easy on the booze.

725
00:32:34,839 --> 00:32:35,319
Jianguo!

726
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:37,319
The stove is still burning.

727
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:37,960
Keep an eye on it for me.

728
00:32:38,319 --> 00:32:38,799
You got it!

729
00:32:39,519 --> 00:32:39,960
Have a seat over here.

730
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,119
It's a bit quieter in this room.

731
00:32:43,599 --> 00:32:44,279
What would you like to eat?

732
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:45,039
I'll whip something up for you.

733
00:32:45,359 --> 00:32:46,240
I've already eaten.

734
00:32:46,880 --> 00:32:48,119
I just wanted to visit you

735
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:49,759
and catch up a bit.

736
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:51,400
All right, then.

737
00:32:52,359 --> 00:32:53,039
I'll brew a pot of tea.

738
00:32:53,920 --> 00:32:54,359
Have a seat.

739
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,039
Thank you.

740
00:32:55,359 --> 00:32:55,799
Sit down.

741
00:33:14,880 --> 00:33:15,480
Come on in.

742
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:20,359
Have a seat, sit down.

743
00:33:22,039 --> 00:33:22,680
Well, uh...

744
00:33:22,799 --> 00:33:23,599
Thank you, thank you.

745
00:33:23,599 --> 00:33:24,839
Please, don't trouble yourself.

746
00:33:25,279 --> 00:33:26,119
The tea isn't anything special.

747
00:33:26,279 --> 00:33:27,400
Just make do with it.

748
00:33:30,599 --> 00:33:31,359
Please sit, please.

749
00:33:38,039 --> 00:33:38,759
So...

750
00:33:40,200 --> 00:33:41,079
you coming to see me,

751
00:33:42,480 --> 00:33:43,240
you must have a reason.

752
00:33:45,319 --> 00:33:46,759
Then I'll just cut to the chase.

753
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,640
The recent murders...

754
00:33:51,359 --> 00:33:52,640
you've heard about them?

755
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:55,480
I have.

756
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,160
Do you think

757
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,119
they have to do with

758
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,240
selling the factory back then?

759
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:09,639
If I said they didn't,

760
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:11,199
would you believe me?

761
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,039
Don't know who it is,

762
00:34:15,599 --> 00:34:16,440
or what's gotten into them,

763
00:34:17,159 --> 00:34:18,239
after all these years,

764
00:34:18,400 --> 00:34:20,000
losing their minds doing this.

765
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,679
Let me tell you,

766
00:34:23,159 --> 00:34:24,559
us old-timers,

767
00:34:25,400 --> 00:34:26,079
our consciences are clear.

768
00:34:29,039 --> 00:34:30,159
Do the other old workers

769
00:34:30,519 --> 00:34:31,559
come around here often too?

770
00:34:33,559 --> 00:34:34,679
Haipeng and his crowd do.

771
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:37,360
Those old bastards are here every day.

772
00:34:40,039 --> 00:34:40,719
Well,

773
00:34:41,039 --> 00:34:44,440
has anyone else asked about back then?

774
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:46,360
Actually, yes.

775
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:47,639
Who?

776
00:34:48,159 --> 00:34:48,800
A cop.

777
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:51,039
The police came by.

778
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:53,360
Older or young?

779
00:34:54,639 --> 00:34:55,480
A young kid.

780
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:57,440
Said his name

781
00:34:58,199 --> 00:34:58,800
was Gao.

782
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:00,320
You know him?

783
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,039
Did he ask about Liu Xuemei?

784
00:35:03,519 --> 00:35:04,719
And what happened the day she died?

785
00:35:05,159 --> 00:35:06,400
That's exactly what he asked.

786
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,800
That's all ancient history.

787
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:14,559
In a flash,

788
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:17,000
over ten years have gone by.

789
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:23,280
Whose turn?

790
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:24,920
You play. Go on, play.

791
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:25,679
Me?

792
00:35:25,679 --> 00:35:26,280
Hold on, don't rush.

793
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:27,079
All right, look at this!

794
00:35:27,679 --> 00:35:28,119
How about that?

795
00:35:28,599 --> 00:35:29,320
Damn good!

796
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:30,079
Three 2s.

797
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:31,320
Hey, hey, you...

798
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:31,760
Pass, pass, pass.

799
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:32,880
Can't beat it, pass!

800
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:33,320
Pass.

801
00:35:33,639 --> 00:35:34,119
Come on...

802
00:35:34,159 --> 00:35:34,679
Can't beat that.

803
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:35,800
Pass.

804
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:37,480
Three 2s!

805
00:35:37,519 --> 00:35:38,360
I win!

806
00:35:38,719 --> 00:35:39,639
You guys...

807
00:35:41,159 --> 00:35:41,559
What in the world...

808
00:35:41,559 --> 00:35:42,159
How could you play like that?

809
00:35:42,639 --> 00:35:43,599
In the first three quarters,

810
00:35:43,719 --> 00:35:44,639
our bottling workshop

811
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,800
came in first again!

812
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:47,679
Great!

813
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:48,360
Old Cheng,

814
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:50,199
you led the way wonderfully!

815
00:35:50,199 --> 00:35:50,760
Didn't he?

816
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:52,440
Absolutely!

817
00:35:53,039 --> 00:35:54,119
Director Tian from the Women's Federation

818
00:35:54,239 --> 00:35:55,440
has taken great care of us.

819
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:56,079
Right?

820
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:57,320
Just doing my job. Come on,

821
00:35:57,960 --> 00:36:00,320
let's toast Director Tian!

822
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:01,400
Cheers!

823
00:36:01,719 --> 00:36:03,000
Director Tian, thank you so much!

824
00:36:03,719 --> 00:36:04,400
As for labor protection gear,

825
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:05,199
hand out extra to everyone!

826
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:06,320
Count on it.

827
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:06,559
Cheers!

828
00:36:06,599 --> 00:36:07,679
Thank you, everyone! Thank you!

829
00:36:09,119 --> 00:36:10,119
Bottoms up! Bottoms up!

830
00:36:57,519 --> 00:36:58,480
Alright, everyone,

831
00:36:59,199 --> 00:37:00,239
let me introduce someone to you.

832
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:02,599
Our factory's new beer taster,

833
00:37:03,280 --> 00:37:04,199
Comrade Liu Xuemei.

834
00:37:05,159 --> 00:37:05,719
Give her a hand!

835
00:37:06,679 --> 00:37:07,519
Welcome, Xuemei!

836
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:11,119
Welcome! Welcome, welcome!

837
00:37:11,239 --> 00:37:12,039
Now, Xuemei,

838
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:13,639
it's your first day here.

839
00:37:14,360 --> 00:37:15,320
Well,

840
00:37:15,880 --> 00:37:16,480
now that you're in the workshop,

841
00:37:17,239 --> 00:37:18,079
we're all family.

842
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:19,519
If you run into any trouble, just speak up.

843
00:37:19,880 --> 00:37:22,079
We older folks will take care of you.

844
00:37:22,199 --> 00:37:22,960
Don't you worry.

845
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:25,599
And, uh...

846
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:26,679
there's one more thing.

847
00:37:27,280 --> 00:37:27,719
What is it?

848
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:29,679
How should I put it?

849
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:30,599
What's the matter?

850
00:37:33,599 --> 00:37:35,159
Lao Cheng, you're utterly hopeless.

851
00:37:35,639 --> 00:37:36,199
I'll say it for you.

852
00:37:40,119 --> 00:37:40,760
Xuemei,

853
00:37:42,239 --> 00:37:44,039
that little skirt looks gorgeous on you.

854
00:37:44,639 --> 00:37:45,920
If I had your figure,

855
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:47,400
I'd wear one every day too.

856
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:48,800
Too bad you don't!

857
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:49,960
What did you say?

858
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:50,840
Get out of here!

859
00:37:52,599 --> 00:37:53,159
Xuemei,

860
00:37:53,679 --> 00:37:54,679
the thing is,

861
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:55,880
our workshop has rules.

862
00:37:56,079 --> 00:37:57,360
Once you're in the workshop,

863
00:37:57,519 --> 00:37:58,639
you have to wear the uniform.

864
00:37:59,239 --> 00:37:59,679
Look,

865
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,400
don't our work clothes look sharp?

866
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:01,880
Right?

867
00:38:03,039 --> 00:38:04,760
I just thought, since it's my first day...

868
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:06,840
It's my fault.

869
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:08,599
I didn't check beforehand.

870
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:10,599
I'm so sorry, everyone.

871
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:23,320
Nice!

872
00:38:23,719 --> 00:38:24,280
Great!

873
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:26,760
What are you doing?

874
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:28,360
You're not a beer taster.

875
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:29,840
Come on, come on.

876
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:30,559
Raise your glasses, pick 'em up!

877
00:38:30,679 --> 00:38:31,519
Come on, Xuemei.

878
00:38:31,639 --> 00:38:32,360
Come on, everyone.

879
00:38:32,719 --> 00:38:33,440
Come on.

880
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:36,119
We're all family here.

881
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:38,320
Let's welcome Liu Xuemei!

882
00:38:38,639 --> 00:38:40,400
Welcome, Liu Xuemei!

883
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:42,079
Welcome, Liu Xuemei!

884
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:43,519
Cheers!

885
00:38:53,559 --> 00:38:54,840
Just because a woman came by,

886
00:38:55,039 --> 00:38:55,840
you're getting restless already?

887
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,760
We're just worried you can't sit still.

888
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:58,760
Why would I be restless?

889
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:02,880
Your wife left with the kid two years ago,

890
00:39:03,199 --> 00:39:05,239
and she hasn't come back since.

891
00:39:06,079 --> 00:39:07,159
You just have to run your mouth, huh?

892
00:39:08,199 --> 00:39:09,559
I've only got myself to feed.

893
00:39:09,920 --> 00:39:10,760
Who gives a damn anyway?

894
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:12,400
Director,

895
00:39:12,639 --> 00:39:13,719
cut the act.

896
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:16,320
We all know Liu Xuemei is divorced too.

897
00:39:16,599 --> 00:39:17,880
Quit playing coy.

898
00:39:17,880 --> 00:39:19,400
You two should just get together.

899
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:20,639
You'd get a ready-made son,

900
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:21,679
how great is that?

901
00:39:22,119 --> 00:39:22,719
Yeah, yeah, right.

902
00:39:23,559 --> 00:39:24,039
Laughing?

903
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,039
What are you laughing at?

904
00:39:25,559 --> 00:39:26,360
What's so funny?

905
00:39:27,480 --> 00:39:27,880
Get back to work.

906
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:28,239
What's wrong?

907
00:39:28,559 --> 00:39:29,360
I'm going.

908
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:29,960
Go on, get to work.

909
00:39:29,960 --> 00:39:30,360
I...

910
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:32,440
Wait, wait, we'll wait for you!

911
00:39:33,239 --> 00:39:33,920
Can't play cards without you!

912
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:34,920
You guys have too much time on your hands.

913
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:44,360
Xuemei, getting water?

914
00:39:44,360 --> 00:39:44,920
Xuemei.

915
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:46,480
Have you eaten?

916
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:47,360
I have.

917
00:39:48,199 --> 00:39:48,719
Xuemei.

918
00:39:49,119 --> 00:39:49,800
Mr. Cheng.

919
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:51,159
Getting water?

920
00:39:52,159 --> 00:39:52,719
Xuemei.

921
00:40:15,199 --> 00:40:16,480
I forgot the tea leaves, Mr. Cheng.

922
00:40:16,679 --> 00:40:17,599
I'll go grab them from the workshop.

923
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:27,920
It's not easy raising a kid on your own.

924
00:40:30,559 --> 00:40:31,000
It's fine.

925
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:31,880
I'm used to it.

926
00:40:34,719 --> 00:40:35,360
Well...

927
00:40:35,639 --> 00:40:36,480
If you ever run into trouble,

928
00:40:37,159 --> 00:40:37,559
just say the word.

929
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:40,400
Thanks, Mr. Cheng.

930
00:40:42,159 --> 00:40:43,079
The guys in the workshop,

931
00:40:43,800 --> 00:40:44,440
they're all pretty rough,

932
00:40:44,599 --> 00:40:45,519
but they've got good hearts.

933
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,559
If there's any gossip going around,

934
00:40:48,199 --> 00:40:48,920
don't take it to heart.

935
00:40:50,039 --> 00:40:51,280
What gossip?

936
00:40:53,239 --> 00:40:53,679
Nothing?

937
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:56,800
Well... all right then.

938
00:40:59,679 --> 00:41:00,960
It's just those punks,

939
00:41:02,639 --> 00:41:04,199
always teasing a bachelor like me.

940
00:41:05,079 --> 00:41:06,119
Whenever a woman comes around,

941
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:07,239
they try to play matchmaker.

942
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,440
Don't let it bother you.

943
00:41:11,679 --> 00:41:13,119
I wouldn't take it to heart.

944
00:41:13,559 --> 00:41:15,119
I can manage my own life.

945
00:41:15,719 --> 00:41:16,519
I don't have any intentions like that,

946
00:41:16,719 --> 00:41:17,440
so don't overthink it either.

947
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:18,639
Didn't take it to heart, huh?

948
00:41:19,719 --> 00:41:20,039
Well,

949
00:41:20,239 --> 00:41:21,039
if you're not interested,

950
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:21,960
that's a relief.

951
00:41:25,639 --> 00:41:26,199
Mr. Cheng,

952
00:41:26,639 --> 00:41:27,280
the water's overflowing.

953
00:41:34,039 --> 00:41:35,199
She's not interested,

954
00:41:39,280 --> 00:41:41,519
and now it feels off.

955
00:42:01,639 --> 00:42:02,159
What's wrong?

956
00:42:03,639 --> 00:42:04,199
No idea.

957
00:42:04,199 --> 00:42:04,800
Looks like he fell asleep.

958
00:42:34,679 --> 00:42:35,679
On the very same day,

959
00:42:36,519 --> 00:42:40,280
both died of alcohol poisoning.

960
00:42:40,519 --> 00:42:41,559
Don't you find that suspicious?

961
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:43,400
Know what to say

962
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,559
and what not to say.

963
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:48,079
Whatever you do, don't slip up.

964
00:42:48,639 --> 00:42:50,519
This has nothing to do with my mentor.

965
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,079
I apologize.

966
00:42:52,280 --> 00:42:53,679
I shouldn't have run my mouth.
